#!/bin/bash
# accounts/help.loc - Module-specific help

cat <<'EOF'
Module: accounts - site groups and user accounts

  Everything root does TO accounts lives here. The unprivileged command
  users run to change their own password lives in the 'pwsync' module.

  RETURNING COLD? Read accounts/README.md first. It explains why the roster
  is static rather than LDAP-backed, why accounts start locked, and what
  state the migration is in. Short version:

    - Users came from LDAP on sun. LDAP is being decommissioned, so the
      directory was harvested ONCE into yamc.local/accounts/*.conf, which
      are now the source of truth.
    - LDAP {SSHA} hashes cannot go into /etc/shadow, so every account is
      created LOCKED and everyone needs a new password once.
    - As of 2026-07-28 this module had been dry-run tested but NEVER
      actually applied to any host. pwsync is deployed and working.
    - This replaces the csync2 plan still described in
      yamc.local/mailserver/README.md. Ignore that plan.

SUBCOMMANDS

  setup                          Provision groups, then users, from the
                                 roster in yamc.local/accounts/.
      yamc -h HOST -u root accounts
      yamc -h HOST -u root -e ACCT_DRYRUN=1 accounts        # preview
      yamc -h HOST -u root -e ACCT_GROUPS_ONLY=1 accounts   # groups only
      yamc -h HOST -u root -e ACCT_USERS="julee,mia" accounts
      yamc -h HOST -u root -e ACCT_FORCE=1 accounts         # ignore UID guard

  setpass USERNAME               Set or reset a password (root). Generates
                                 a random one and prints it once, so no
                                 secret travels inbound.
      yamc -h HOST -u root accounts setpass julee
      yamc -h HOST -u root -e ACCT_PROMPT=1 accounts setpass julee
      yamc -h HOST -u root -e ACCT_EXPIRE=1 accounts setpass julee

  adduser USERNAME               Look up one straggler in LDAP and create
                                 them. Prints the roster line to paste into
                                 users.conf.
      yamc -h HOST -u root accounts adduser someone

CLUSTER HELPERS  (yamc.local/bin/)

  accounts-cluster-deploy        Provision every host in the cluster
  accounts-cluster-setpass USER  Reset a password on every host

ROSTER  (yamc.local/accounts/)

  groups.conf    name:gid
                 gid of '-' means a distribution system group: never
                 create it, only add members. LDAP's audio=63 conflicts
                 with Ubuntu's audio=29, which is why this exists.

  users.conf     user:uid:gid:gecos:home:shell:supplementary_groups
                 Group membership lives here, so adding a person is one
                 line. UIDs are pinned because /home is NFS-shared.

  ldap.conf      Only for 'adduser'. Delete when sun is decommissioned.

SAFETY

  Home directories are NEVER created (useradd -M): /home is NFS-mounted and
  already holds the users' files.

  Before creating an account, the existing home directory is checked:
    UID mismatch -> hard failure (the user could not read their own files)
    GID mismatch -> warning only (a home group-owned by a shared group,
                    such as /home/mia being 1005:1500, is normal)

  Accounts are created LOCKED. LDAP {SSHA} hashes are not a crypt(3) format
  and cannot be migrated. Use setpass, then have the user run pwsync.
EOF
